        "parameters": {
          "content": "## Skip unchanged documents\nHashes each doc's extracted text (SHA-256) and compares to what's already stored. Unchanged docs are filtered out right here -- nothing downstream (chunking, embedding, DB writes) re-runs for them.\n\nFiltering happens in a Code node, not a SQL WHERE guard -- see PLAN.md's M1 section for why (a real bug: Postgres nodes here collapse to one ambiguous item when every row in a batch returns zero results).",
          "height": 220,
          "width": 660,
          "color": 5
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "note-throttle",
        "name": "Sticky Note - Throttle",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          2000,
          620
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "content": "## Sequential on purpose\nOllama (CPU, self-hosted) only has one processing slot. Firing embedding requests concurrently queues them behind each other until n8n's own timeout kills them -- this loop (batch size 1) keeps them strictly sequential instead. The HTTP node's own \"batching\" option did NOT achieve this in testing; this Split In Batches loop did.",
          "height": 220,
          "width": 660,
          "color": 3
        }
